# bmc-ui-*.tar.gz is a GitHub RELEASE ASSET, not a tag archive: a release
# asset can be re-uploaded under the same name, and GitHub exposes no digest
# for it. Pinned on purpose -- if the asset ever changes, the build fails here
# instead of silently shipping a different UI.
#
# This is our fork's release, not upstream's. Upstream v3.3.7 rendered
# "vundefined" for the build version, reported the firmware name as the
# Buildroot release, shipped 668.9 KB of fonts including 21 .woff files no
# browser that can run the bundle needs, and -- despite bmc-ui.mk declaring
# BMC_UI_LICENSE_FILES = LICENSE -- shipped no LICENSE at all, which for a
# GPL-2.0 work we redistribute was a real gap. Ours carries it.
#
# Verified 2026-09-09: 577994 bytes, built by GitHub Actions from tag
# v3.17.0. The sum was recomputed from the downloaded bytes rather than read
# out of the release's own SHA256SUMS -- a manifest published beside an asset
# cannot attest to it, and catching a re-uploaded asset is the whole reason
# this file exists.
#
# v3.16.0 folded the pages' standing explanations behind (i) popovers that
# link to the docs site. v3.17.0 removed the Metrics token card: /metrics
# moved to its own credential-free listener, so there is no token to show or
# rotate, and a card offering to rotate one would imply a protection that is
# not there.
#
# The sum is UNCHANGED across the move to excavador-turing. The asset was
# rebuilt from the same tree under the new owner and came out byte-identical
# -- 573360 bytes, same sha256 -- because the release workflow packs with
# `tar --sort=name | gzip -9 -n`, which pins member order and drops the
# gzip timestamp. Only the URL in bmc-ui.mk changed.
sha256  59b4495e3405dc6469e666b7d782040912f370eef12fe0c41443d0403c80933b  bmc-ui-v3.17.0.tar.gz
